# NUMERICS: `%` on two integers is FLOORED — the remainder takes the DIVISOR's
# sign — and it does so whatever shape the divisor arrives in. THE DIVISOR'S
# SHAPE IS THIS FILE'S HALF: every row below is the same arithmetic reached
# through a different divisor shape — positive literal, negative literal, and a
# value the emitter cannot read — so a rule that holds for one shape and not
# another cannot pass here. The sign matrix itself is measured by
# `examples/table/divsign.id` (realized) and `examples/table/div/sign.id`
# (folded), which also carry `//`, the operator the same ruling settled.
#
# THIS HEADER'S CITATION IS RETRACTED, and it is the SECOND one this file has
# lost. It cited `§12 B-4` for a TRUNCATING `%` and pinned `-1 1 -1 1 -1 1`;
# `§12 B-4` exists in no document. It then cited `docs/rulings.md`
# § "Modulo and floor division" for the floored law, and
# `git log --all --diff-filter=A -- docs/rulings.md` IS EMPTY — that document
# has never been added on any branch of this repository. Nothing that opens
# carries the law today, and the compiler's own `law §62` opens on EVIDENCE MUST
# BE PRIVATE TO THE RUN. `examples/table/divsign.id` states the measurement and
# names what is still pointing at what.
#
# THE `cbackend` HOME IS NOT REACH, and this file is the proof. Measured at this
# tip, every row here refuses on the backend the directory names:
#
#   idol compile --backend=c --emit=c examples/cbackend/modsign.id
#   error: C99 realizer: no realization (UnsupportedProgram)
#   hint: refused at: binop-not-in-c99-slice
#   hint: in relation: main
#
# `emitBinop` admits `+ - *` and the six comparisons and nothing else, so `%`,
# `//` and `/` are all outside the slice — `+`, `-` and `*` emit C through the
# same command, which is the control that the refusal is the slice boundary and
# not a broken file. The direct backend answers DNB004 on this host. The `%`
# columns below are therefore measured on `--backend=wasm` under wasmtime, and
# that is the ONLY realization in this tree that answers them.
#
# Computed by hand from Lua 5.4 §3.4.1, `a % b == a - floor(a/b)*b`:
#   -7 % 2 = -7 - (-4 * 2) = 1.   7 % -2 = 7 - (-4 * -2) = -1.
# Measured by `gate/divsign.sh`.
# expect: 1 -1 1 -1 1 -1
# @corpus current
two = 2
neg = 0 - two
a = -7 % 2
b = 7 % -2
c = -7 % two
d = 7 % neg
e = 0 - 7
f = e % two
g = 7 % neg
print("{a} {b} {c} {d} {f} {g}")
0
